# Line endings are LF everywhere. These scripts run on a Linux cluster, where a
# CR at the end of a shebang or an assignment is part of the value, so a file
# that picks up CRLF on a Windows checkout - or from an editor or a tool that
# rewrites it - is a file that no longer runs. Committing LF is not enough on
# its own: eol=lf makes the checkout LF too, so the working copy matches what
# runs.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text; the image rules below keep it from
# having to guess.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.qza binary
*.rds binary
